{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>But one shall stand</b> — from her roots. The mem in וְעָמַד will serve for one of the sons of the king of Egypt, and he is the king's son." "<b>And he shall come</b> — against the king of the north and into the fortress of his stronghold."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The comment is terse and somewhat elliptical: Ibn Ezra addresses the plural suffix in וְעָמַדָהּ by arguing the prefixed mem effectively stands for 'one of' her offspring."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:56.984207457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}